= Fine-Tuning
<fine-tuning>
== Introduction to Fine-Tuning
<introduction-to-fine-tuning>
#block[
#strong[Definition 1] (Fine-Tuning). #emph[Fine-tuning is the process of
taking a pre-trained language model and adapting it to a specific task
or domain by continuing training on a smaller, task-specific dataset.
This approach leverages transfer learning to utilize the general
language understanding already acquired during pre-training.]

]
#strong[Theoretical Foundation:]

Fine-tuning operates on the principle of #strong[transfer learning];,
where a model trained on a large, general corpus (pre-training)
transfers its learned representations to a specific downstream task.
Mathematically, we can express this as:

$ theta_(f i n e - t u n e d) = theta_(p r e - t r a i n e d) + Delta theta $

Where:

- $theta_(p r e - t r a i n e d)$: Initial weights from pre-training

- $Delta theta$: Weight updates during fine-tuning

- $theta_(f i n e - t u n e d)$: Final adapted weights

#strong[Loss Function:]

For causal language modeling (like GPT-2), the objective is to minimize
the negative log-likelihood:

$ cal(L) \( theta \) = - sum_(i = 1)^N log P_theta \( x_i \| x_(< i) \) $

Where $x_i$ is the $i$-th token and $x_(< i)$ represents all preceding
tokens.

=== Key Concepts
<key-concepts>
- #strong[Transfer Learning];: Leveraging knowledge from source task
  (pre-training) to target task (fine-tuning)

- #strong[Task Adaptation];: Specializing the model for specific tasks
  (e.g., medical Q&A, code generation)

- #strong[Full Parameter Updates];: All model parameters ($theta$) are
  updated during training

- #strong[Computational Cost];: $O \( n \)$ memory where $n$ is total
  parameter count

- #strong[Catastrophic Forgetting];: Risk of losing pre-trained
  knowledge

#figure(image("../visualization/images/fine_tuning/transfer_learning_process.png", width: 95.0%),
  caption: [
    Transfer Learning Process: From Pre-training to Fine-tuning to
    Adapted Model
  ]
)
<fig:transfer_learning>

=== When to Use Fine-Tuning
<when-to-use-fine-tuning>
