== Advantages and Disadvantages
<advantages-and-disadvantages>
=== Advantages
<advantages>
- #strong[Full Adaptation];: All parameters updated for maximum task
  performance

- #strong[Best Performance];: Often achieves highest accuracy on
  specific tasks

- #strong[Flexibility];: Can modify any layer or component

=== Disadvantages
<disadvantages>
- #strong[High Memory Requirements];: Requires GPU memory for all
  parameters

- #strong[Storage];: Need to save entire model (~500MB for GPT-2)

- #strong[Computational Cost];: Slower training compared to
  parameter-efficient methods

- #strong[Catastrophic Forgetting];: May lose general knowledge from
  pre-training

