== Extended Theory: Fine-Tuning Deep Dive
<extended-theory-fine-tuning-deep-dive>
=== Mathematical Foundation of Transfer Learning
<mathematical-foundation-of-transfer-learning>
Transfer learning in fine-tuning can be formalized through the lens of
domain adaptation theory. Consider two probability distributions:

$ cal(D)_s & : upright("Source domain (pre-training data)")\
cal(D)_t & : upright("Target domain (fine-tuning data)") $

The goal of fine-tuning is to minimize the expected loss on the target
domain:

$ theta^(*) = arg min_theta bb(E)_(\( x \, y \) tilde.op cal(D)_t) \[ cal(L) \( f_theta \( x \) \, y \) \] $

where we initialize $theta$ from pre-training rather than randomly.

#strong[Why This Works - Ben-David et al. Domain Adaptation Theory:]

The error on target domain $epsilon.alt_t \( theta \)$ is bounded by:

$ epsilon.alt_t \( theta \) lt.eq epsilon.alt_s \( theta \) + d_(cal(H)) \( cal(D)_s \, cal(D)_t \) + lambda $

where:

- $epsilon.alt_s \( theta \)$: Source domain error (achieved during
  pre-training)

- $d_(cal(H)) \( cal(D)_s \, cal(D)_t \)$: Domain divergence (how
  different distributions are)

- $lambda$: Error of ideal joint hypothesis on both domains

#strong[Implication:] If source model performs well ($epsilon.alt_s$
low) and domains are not too different ($d_(cal(H))$ small), fine-tuning
will succeed on target domain.

=== Learning Rate Schedules for Fine-Tuning
<learning-rate-schedules-for-fine-tuning>
Unlike training from scratch, fine-tuning requires careful learning rate
management:

#strong[\1. Discriminative Learning Rates (Differential Learning):]

Different layers learn at different rates:

$ eta_l = eta_0 dot.op gamma^(L - l) $

where:

- $eta_l$: Learning rate for layer $l$

- $eta_0$: Base learning rate

- $gamma$: Decay factor (typically 0.95)

- $L$: Total number of layers

#strong[Intuition:] Earlier layers capture general features; later
layers capture task-specific patterns. Use lower learning rates for
earlier layers to preserve pre-trained knowledge.

#strong[\2. Warm-up + Cosine Annealing:]

$ eta_t = cases(delim: "{", eta_(m a x) dot.op t / T_(w a r m u p) & upright("if ") t < T_(w a r m u p), eta_(m i n) + 1 / 2 \( eta_(m a x) - eta_(m i n) \) \( 1 + cos \( frac(t - T_(w a r m u p), T - T_(w a r m u p)) pi \) \) & upright("otherwise")) $

#strong[Typical values for fine-tuning:]

- $eta_(m a x) = 3 times 10^(- 5)$ (3x lower than pre-training)

- $T_(w a r m u p) = 0.1 times T$ (10% of total steps)

- $eta_(m i n) = 0$ or $10^(- 6)$

