#strong[Interpretation of Fisher Values:]

- #strong[High Fisher ($F_(i i) > 0.1$):] Parameter is critical for Task
  A. Changing it will hurt Task A performance significantly. EWC
  strongly penalizes changes.

- #strong[Medium Fisher ($0.01 < F_(i i) < 0.1$):] Parameter contributes
  moderately. Some adaptation allowed but with penalty.

- #strong[Low Fisher ($F_(i i) < 0.01$):] Parameter is not important for
  Task A. Can be freely adapted for Task B without forgetting Task A.

#strong[Trade-off Parameter $lambda$:]

The EWC strength parameter $lambda$ controls the forgetting-adaptation
trade-off:

$ lambda = 0 quad arrow.r.double quad upright("No protection, maximum forgetting") $
$ lambda arrow.r oo quad arrow.r.double quad upright("Complete protection, no adaptation") $

Typical values: $lambda in \[ 100 \, 10000 \]$ depending on tasks.

