#strong[\1. Learning Rate Selection - The Most Critical Hyperparameter:]

#strong[Theoretical Guidance:]

The optimal learning rate depends on the Lipschitz constant $L$ of the
loss gradient:

$ eta_(o p t) lt.eq 1 / L quad upright("where ") L = max_(theta_1 \, theta_2) frac(parallel nabla cal(L) \( theta_1 \) - nabla cal(L) \( theta_2 \) parallel, parallel theta_1 - theta_2 parallel) $

In practice, $L$ is unknown, but we can estimate it from pre-training
statistics.

