#strong[\3. Number of Epochs - Avoiding Overfitting:]

#strong[Early Stopping Criterion:]

Monitor validation loss; stop when it increases for $p$ consecutive
checks:

$ upright("Stop if: ") cal(L)_(v a l) \( t \) > cal(L)_(v a l) \( t - 1 \) > dots.h > cal(L)_(v a l) \( t - p + 1 \) $

Typical: $p = 3$ to $5$ checks.

#strong[Dataset Size Guidelines:]

$ N < 1000 & : upright("Epochs") in \[ 10 \, 20 \] \, upright("high risk of overfitting")\
1000 lt.eq N < 10000 & : upright("Epochs") in \[ 5 \, 10 \] \, upright("monitor validation")\
10000 lt.eq N < 100000 & : upright("Epochs") in \[ 3 \, 5 \] \, upright("less overfitting risk")\
N gt.eq 100000 & : upright("Epochs") in \[ 1 \, 3 \] \, upright("minimal overfitting") $

#strong[Overfitting Detection:]

Train/validation loss gap:

$ upright("Gap") = cal(L)_(t r a i n) - cal(L)_(v a l) $

- $upright("Gap") < 0.1$: Healthy, can train more

- $0.1 lt.eq upright("Gap") < 0.5$: Slight overfitting, monitor closely

- $upright("Gap") gt.eq 0.5$: Significant overfitting, stop or
  regularize

#strong[\4. Weight Decay (L2 Regularization):]

Modified loss with weight decay:

$ cal(L)_(t o t a l) \( theta \) = cal(L)_(d a t a) \( theta \) + lambda_(W D) / 2 parallel theta parallel^2 $

Gradient update with AdamW:

$ theta_(t + 1) = theta_t - eta nabla cal(L)_(d a t a) \( theta_t \) - eta lambda_(W D) theta_t $

