=== Tokenization Strategies
<tokenization-strategies>
#strong[\1. Byte Pair Encoding (BPE):]

Iteratively merge most frequent character pairs:

#block[
$V arrow.l$ {all characters} $\( c_1 \, c_2 \) arrow.l$ most frequent
consecutive pair $V arrow.l V union { c_1 c_2 }$ Replace all
$\( c_1 \, c_2 \)$ with $c_1 c_2$ in corpus

]
#strong[Advantages:]

- No unknown tokens (can always fall back to characters)

- Data-driven vocabulary

- Balances word-level and character-level

#strong[\2. WordPiece (BERT):]

Similar to BPE but merges based on likelihood increase:

$ upright("score") \( c_1 \, c_2 \) = frac(upright("freq") \( c_1 c_2 \), upright("freq") \( c_1 \) times upright("freq") \( c_2 \)) $

#strong[\3. SentencePiece (T5, GPT-2):]

Treats input as raw UTF-8 byte stream, allows subword units:

- Reversible tokenization

- Language-independent

- Handles spaces as special character (underscore symbol)

