#strong[Explanation:] The weights are initialized randomly with std
$approx 0.02$ (matching `initializer_range=0.02`). This initialization
is critical - too large and gradients explode, too small and they
vanish.

The initialization scheme for layer $l$ is typically:

$ W_l tilde.op cal(N) (0 \, sigma^2 / n_(i n)) quad upright("or") quad W_l tilde.op cal(U) (- 1 / sqrt(n_(i n)) \, 1 / sqrt(n_(i n))) $

where $n_(i n)$ is the input dimension (Xavier/Glorot initialization).
This keeps activation magnitudes stable across layers.

