#strong[Impact on Model Performance:]

For a neural network layer:

$ y = W x + b $

Quantized version:

$ tilde(y) = Q \( W \) x + b = \( W + epsilon.alt_W \) x + b = y + epsilon.alt_W x $

#strong[Error propagation:]

$ upright("Output error: ") parallel tilde(y) - y parallel^2 & = parallel epsilon.alt_W x parallel^2\
 & lt.eq parallel epsilon.alt_W parallel_F^2 parallel x parallel^2\
 & approx Delta^2 / 12 dot.op d dot.op k dot.op parallel x parallel^2 $

where $d times k$ is the weight matrix dimension.

#strong[Critical Insight for QLoRA:]

For large models (e.g., $d = k = 4096$):

$ upright("Accumulated error") prop sqrt(d dot.op k) dot.op Delta = sqrt(16 M) dot.op Delta = 4000 dot.op Delta $

This is why #strong[NF4 (information-theoretically optimal
quantization)] is crucial: it reduces $Delta$ by $approx$35% compared to
uniform Int4, which translates to 35% reduction in accumulated error!

