= PEFT - Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning
<peft---parameter-efficient-fine-tuning>
== Introduction to PEFT
<introduction-to-peft>
#strong[PEFT (Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning)] is a collection of
techniques that enable efficient adaptation of large pre-trained models
by training only a small number of additional parameters while keeping
most of the model frozen. The Hugging Face PEFT library provides a
unified framework for various methods including LoRA, Prefix Tuning,
P-Tuning, and Prompt Tuning.

=== Key Concepts
<key-concepts-4>
- #strong[Unified Framework];: Single library supporting multiple PEFT
  methods

- #strong[Adapter Architecture];: Modular design for easy switching

- #strong[Memory Efficiency];: Train large models with limited resources

- #strong[Model Modularity];: Multiple adapters for different tasks

- #strong[Easy Integration];: Compatible with Transformers library

== PEFT Methods Overview
<peft-methods-overview>
=== 1. LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation)
<lora-low-rank-adaptation>
- Adds trainable rank decomposition matrices

- Most popular PEFT method

- Trains 0.1-1% of parameters

- Best balance of efficiency and performance

=== 2. Prefix Tuning
<prefix-tuning>
- Prepends trainable prefix vectors to each layer

- Modifies only the prefix, not the model

- Effective for generation tasks

- 0.1-3% parameters typically

=== 3. P-Tuning
<p-tuning>
- Learns continuous prompts via neural networks

- Optimizes prompt embeddings

- Good for few-shot learning

- Very parameter efficient

=== 4. Prompt Tuning
<prompt-tuning>
- Adds trainable tokens to input

- Simplest PEFT method

- Only prompt embeddings trained

- Works well for large models (11B+)

=== 5. Adapter Layers
<adapter-layers>
- Inserts small bottleneck layers

- Classic PEFT approach

- Adds parameters between transformer layers

- Easy to understand and implement

== PEFT Library Architecture
<peft-library-architecture>
```
Base Model (Frozen)
     |
     v
PEFT Config (LoRA/Prefix/P-Tuning/etc.)
     |
     v
PEFT Model (Base + Adapters)
     |
     v
Training (Only Adapters Updated)
     |
     v
Save Adapters (~5-50 MB)
     |
     v
Load Base + Adapters for Inference
```

