== PEFT Best Practices
<peft-best-practices>
=== Choosing the Right Method
<choosing-the-right-method>
- #strong[LoRA];: Best general-purpose method, works for most tasks

- #strong[Prefix Tuning];: Good for generation tasks (summarization,
  translation)

- #strong[P-Tuning];: Effective for understanding tasks (classification,
  QA)

- #strong[Prompt Tuning];: Best for very large models (11B+ parameters)

=== Hyperparameter Guidelines
<hyperparameter-guidelines>
- #strong[LoRA Rank (r)];: Start with 8-16, increase if underperforming

- #strong[LoRA Alpha];: Typically $2 times r$ (e.g., r=8 $arrow.r$
  alpha=16)

- #strong[Learning Rate];: 3e-4 to 1e-3 (higher than full fine-tuning)

- #strong[Dropout];: 0.05-0.1 for regularization

- #strong[Target Modules];: Attention layers for most impact

== Advantages of PEFT Framework
<advantages-of-peft-framework>
- #strong[Unified API];: Consistent interface across methods

- #strong[Easy Switching];: Try different methods with minimal code
  changes

- #strong[Memory Efficient];: Train large models on consumer GPUs

- #strong[Storage Efficient];: Share base model, distribute small
  adapters

- #strong[Fast Experimentation];: Quick iteration on different
  approaches

- #strong[Production Ready];: Mature library with good documentation

- #strong[Community Support];: Active development and examples

== Use Cases and Applications
<use-cases-and-applications>
- #strong[Multi-Task Learning];: Different adapters for different tasks

- #strong[Personalization];: User-specific adapters

- #strong[Domain Adaptation];: Industry-specific fine-tuning

- #strong[Continual Learning];: Add adapters without forgetting

- #strong[A/B Testing];: Quickly test different fine-tuning strategies

- #strong[Resource-Constrained Deployment];: Fine-tune on limited
  hardware

== Extended Theory: PEFT Methods Comprehensive Analysis
<extended-theory-peft-methods-comprehensive-analysis>
=== Taxonomy of Parameter-Efficient Methods
<taxonomy-of-parameter-efficient-methods>
PEFT methods can be categorized into four main families:

#strong[\1. Additive Methods (Add new parameters):]

- #strong[Adapters:] Insert trainable bottleneck layers

- #strong[Soft Prompts:] Add trainable token embeddings

- #strong[LoRA:] Add low-rank update matrices

#strong[\2. Selective Methods (Select subset to train):]

- #strong[BitFit:] Train only bias terms

- #strong[Child-Tuning:] Dynamically select parameters

#strong[\3. Reparameterization Methods:]

- #strong[LoRA:] Low-rank decomposition

- #strong[Compacter:] Kronecker products

#strong[\4. Hybrid Methods:]

- #strong[UniPELT:] Combine multiple PEFT methods

- #strong[MAM Adapter:] Mix attention and LoRA

=== Prefix Tuning: Mathematical Foundation
<prefix-tuning-mathematical-foundation>
#strong[Concept:] Prepend trainable continuous vectors to input
sequence.

#strong[Standard Transformer:]

$ upright("Attention") \( Q \, K \, V \) = upright("softmax") (frac(Q K^T, sqrt(d_k))) V $

#strong[Prefix Tuning:]

$ K_(p r e f i x) & = \[ P_K ; K \] \, quad V_(p r e f i x) = \[ P_V ; V \]\
upright("Attention") \( Q \, K_(p r e f i x) \, V_(p r e f i x) \) & = upright("softmax") (frac(Q \[ P_K ; K \]^T, sqrt(d_k))) \[ P_V ; V \] $

where $P_K \, P_V in bb(R)^(l times d)$ are trainable prefix parameters
($l$ = prefix length).

#strong[Parameter Count:]

$ N_(p r e f i x) = 2 times L times l times d $

where $L$ = number of layers, $l$ = prefix length (typically 10-20), $d$
\= hidden dimension.

#strong[Example (GPT-2, $l = 20$):]

$ N_(p r e f i x) = 2 times 12 times 20 times 768 = 368 \, 640 upright(" params") approx 0.3 % $

=== Prompt Tuning: Simplification of Prefix Tuning
<prompt-tuning-simplification-of-prefix-tuning>
#strong[Difference:] Only add trainable embeddings to input layer (not
every layer).

#strong[Mathematical Form:]

$ upright("Input") = \[ P_(e m b e d) ; E \( x_1 \) ; E \( x_2 \) ; dots.h ; E \( x_n \) \] $

where $P_(e m b e d) in bb(R)^(l times d)$ are soft prompt embeddings.

#strong[Parameter Count:]

$ N_(p r o m p t) = l times d $

#strong[Example (GPT-2, $l = 20$):]

$ N_(p r o m p t) = 20 times 768 = 15 \, 360 upright(" params") approx 0.01 % $

#strong[Scaling Discovery:] Prompt tuning becomes competitive with
fine-tuning only at 10B+ parameters!

=== Adapter Layers: Original PEFT Approach
<adapter-layers-original-peft-approach>
#strong[Architecture:]

Insert bottleneck layers between Transformer sub-layers:

$ h' = h + upright("Adapter") \( h \) $

#strong[Adapter Function:]

$ upright("Adapter") \( h \) = W_(u p) dot.op sigma \( W_(d o w n) dot.op h \) $

where:

- $W_(d o w n) in bb(R)^(r times d)$: Down-projection

- $W_(u p) in bb(R)^(d times r)$: Up-projection

- $r lt.double d$: Bottleneck dimension

#strong[Parameter Count per Layer:]

$ N_(a d a p t e r) = 2 r d + r + d approx 2 r d $

#strong[Comparison with LoRA:]

#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: 3,
    align: (left,center,center,),
    table.header([#strong[Property];], [#strong[Adapter];], [#strong[LoRA];],),
    table.hline(),
