=== Multi-Task Learning with PEFT
<multi-task-learning-with-peft>
#strong[Scenario:] Train single base model on $T$ tasks.

#strong[Traditional Approach:]

$ min_(theta_1 \, dots.h \, theta_T) sum_(i = 1)^T cal(L)_i \( theta_i \) $

Storage: $T times \| W \|$ parameters.

#strong[PEFT Approach:]

$ min_(Delta_1 \, dots.h \, Delta_T) sum_(i = 1)^T cal(L)_i \( W_0 + Delta_i \) $

Storage: $\| W_0 \| + T times \| Delta \|$ parameters.

#strong[Example (10 tasks, GPT-2):]

- Full FT: $10 times 500 upright("MB") = 5 upright("GB")$

- LoRA:
  $500 upright("MB") + 10 times 5 upright("MB") = 550 upright("MB")$ (9x
  reduction!)

=== Interference and Task Arithmetic
<interference-and-task-arithmetic>
Recent discovery: PEFT adapters can be arithmetically combined!

#strong[Task Arithmetic Operations:]

$ upright("Task Addition:") quad & Delta_(c o m b i n e d) = Delta_A + Delta_B\
upright("Task Negation:") quad & Delta_(f o r g e t) = W_0 - lambda Delta_A\
upright("Task Interpolation:") quad & Delta_(m i x) = alpha Delta_A + \( 1 - alpha \) Delta_B $

#strong[Example Applications:]

- Combine sentiment + summarization adapters

- Remove toxic behavior:
  $Delta_(s a f e) = Delta_(b a s e) - lambda Delta_(t o x i c)$

- Smooth transition between tasks during deployment

#strong[Theoretical Justification:]

If adapters operate in orthogonal subspaces:

$ angle.l Delta_A \, Delta_B angle.r_F approx 0 arrow.r.double upright("minimal interference") $

#strong[Empirical Orthogonality:]

$ upright("Interference") = frac(parallel Delta_A Delta_B^T parallel_F, parallel Delta_A parallel_F parallel Delta_B parallel_F) $

Measured: $upright("Interference") approx 0.05$ for diverse tasks (95%
orthogonal!).

