=== LCEL (LangChain Expression Language) Theory
<lcel-langchain-expression-language-theory>
#strong[Runnable Abstraction:]

#block[
#strong[Definition 5] (Runnable). #emph[A Runnable is a callable with
signature: $ R : upright("Input") arrow.r upright("Output") $ supporting
methods: `invoke`, `stream`, `batch`, `ainvoke`.]

]
#strong[Category Theory Perspective:]

Runnables form a category where:

- Objects are data types (Input/Output)

- Morphisms are Runnables

- Composition is pipe operator $\|$

#strong[Composition Law:]

$ \( R_1 \| R_2 \) \| R_3 = R_1 \| \( R_2 \| R_3 \) $

#strong[Identity Law:]

$ R \| upright("Identity") = upright("Identity") \| R = R $

#strong[Parallel Execution:]

Using `RunnableParallel`:

$ R_parallel \( x \) = { k_1 : R_1 \( x \) \, k_2 : R_2 \( x \) \, dots.h \, k_n : R_n \( x \) } $

Execution time:

$ T_parallel = max_(i = 1)^n T_i \( R_i \) $

vs. sequential:

$ T_(upright("seq")) = sum_(i = 1)^n T_i \( R_i \) $

#strong[Speedup:]

$ upright("Speedup") = T_(upright("seq")) / T_parallel = frac(sum_(i = 1)^n T_i, max_(i = 1)^n T_i) $

#strong[Streaming Theory:]

Output stream $cal(S)$:

$ cal(S) = { s_1 \, s_2 \, dots.h \, s_n } $

where $s_i$ arrives at time $t_i$.

Time to first token (TTFT):

$ upright("TTFT") = t_1 $

Tokens per second:

$ upright("TPS") = frac(n, t_n - t_1) $

#strong[Retry with Exponential Backoff:]

Wait time after $i$-th failure:

$ w_i = min \( w_max \, w_0 dot.op 2^(i - 1) \) $

Expected total wait for success probability $p$:

$ bb(E) \[ W \] = sum_(i = 1)^oo \( 1 - p \)^(i - 1) p dot.op sum_(j = 1)^(i - 1) w_j $

#strong[Fallback Chain:]

Try models in order until success:

$ R_(upright("fallback")) = R_1 upright(" or else ") R_2 upright(" or else ") dots.h upright(" or else ") R_n $

Success probability:

$ P \( upright("success") \) = 1 - product_(i = 1)^n \( 1 - p_i \) $

where $p_i = P \( R_i upright(" succeeds") \)$.

