#strong[Checkpoint Compression:]

Store only deltas:

$ upright("CP")_t = upright("CP")_(t - 1) + Delta_t $

where $Delta_t = s_t minus.circle s_(t - 1)$ (set difference).

Compressed storage:

$ upright("Storage")_(upright("delta")) = \| s_0 \| + sum_(t = 1)^T \| Delta_t \| $

typically $\| Delta_t \| lt.double \| s_t \|$.

#strong[Time-Travel Complexity:]

Restoring state at time $t$ from delta checkpoints:

$ s_t = s_0 xor Delta_1 xor Delta_2 xor dots.h xor Delta_t $

has cost $O \( t \)$.

#strong[Checkpoint Frequency Optimization:]

Balance storage cost vs. restore cost. Save every $k$ steps:

$ upright("Cost")_(upright("total")) = T / k dot.op C_(upright("save")) + k / 2 dot.op C_(upright("restore")) $

Optimal $k^(*)$:

$ k^(*) = sqrt(frac(2 T dot.op C_(upright("save")), C_(upright("restore")))) $

=== Multi-Agent System Theory
<multi-agent-system-theory>
#strong[Agent Network:]

System of $n$ agents:

$ cal(A) = { A_1 \, A_2 \, dots.h \, A_n } $

#strong[Communication Graph:]

$G_(upright("comm")) = \( A \, E_(upright("comm")) \)$ where
$\( A_i \, A_j \) in E_(upright("comm"))$ if $A_i$ can send messages to
$A_j$.

#strong[Message Passing:]

Agent $A_i$ sends message $m$ to $A_j$:

$ m : A_i arrow.r A_j $

#strong[Broadcast:]

$ m : A_i arrow.r { A_j : \( A_i \, A_j \) in E_(upright("comm")) } $

#strong[Supervisor Pattern:]

One supervisor $A_0$, $n$ workers ${ A_1 \, dots.h \, A_n }$:

$ upright("Task") & arrow.r A_0\
A_0 & arrow.r A_i quad upright("(assign subtask)")\
A_i & arrow.r A_0 quad upright("(return result)")\
A_0 & arrow.r upright("Output") quad upright("(aggregate)") $

#strong[Load Balancing:]

Supervisor assigns task to agent minimizing:

$ i^(*) = "arg min"_(i = 1)^n \( T_i + W_i \) $

where $T_i$ is agent $i$'s processing time, $W_i$ is current workload.

#strong[Consensus Protocol:]

Agents reach consensus on value $v$:

$ v_(upright("final")) = upright("Aggregate") \( { v_1 \, v_2 \, dots.h \, v_n } \) $

Common aggregation:

- Majority vote: $v_(upright("final")) = upright("mode") \( { v_i } \)$

- Average: $v_(upright("final")) = 1 / n sum_(i = 1)^n v_i$

- Weighted: $v_(upright("final")) = sum_(i = 1)^n w_i v_i$ where
  $sum w_i = 1$

#strong[Byzantine Fault Tolerance:]

With $f$ faulty agents, need $n gt.eq 3 f + 1$ agents for consensus.

#strong[Communication Complexity:]

For all-to-all communication:

$ upright("Messages") = O \( n^2 \) $

For star topology (supervisor):

$ upright("Messages") = O \( n \) $

=== Human-in-the-Loop Theory
<human-in-the-loop-theory>
#strong[Interrupt Points:]

Set of nodes requiring human approval:

$ V_(upright("interrupt")) subset.eq V $

#strong[Wait Time:]

Expected wait for human response:

$ bb(E) \[ T_(upright("wait")) \] = integral_0^oo t dot.op f_(upright("response")) \( t \) thin d t $

where $f_(upright("response")) \( t \)$ is response time distribution.

#strong[Timeout Strategy:]

If no response within time $tau$:

$ lambda \( v \, s \) = cases(delim: "{", v_(upright("human")) \( s \) & upright("if ") t < tau, v_(upright("default")) & upright("if ") t gt.eq tau) $

#strong[Human Override Probability:]

Given agent suggestion $a_(upright("agent"))$, human chooses
$a_(upright("human"))$:

$ P \( upright("override") \) = P \( a_(upright("human")) eq.not a_(upright("agent")) \) $

#strong[Trust Calibration:]

Over time, adjust automation:

$ alpha_t = alpha_(t - 1) + eta dot.op \( 1 - P_t \( upright("override") \) \) $

where $alpha_t in \[ 0 \, 1 \]$ is automation level, $eta$ is learning
rate.

When $alpha_t$ high → fewer interrupts.

#strong[Cost-Benefit Analysis:]

Expected value of human input:

$ V_(upright("human")) = P \( upright("correct") \| upright("human") \) dot.op R_(upright("correct")) - C_(upright("wait")) $

Only interrupt if $V_(upright("human")) > V_(upright("auto"))$.

=== Performance Optimization Theory
<performance-optimization-theory>
#strong[\1. Streaming Latency]

Time to produce $k$-th token:

$ T_k = T_(upright("TTFT")) + \( k - 1 \) dot.op T_(upright("token")) $

where $T_(upright("TTFT"))$ is time to first token,
$T_(upright("token"))$ is inter-token latency.

#strong[Streaming Throughput:]

$ upright("Throughput") = 1 / T_(upright("token")) quad upright("tokens/second") $

#strong[\2. Parallel Execution]

For independent nodes ${ v_1 \, dots.h \, v_k }$:

$ T_parallel = max_(i = 1)^k T_i + O \( upright("sync") \) $

#strong[Amdahl's Law for Graphs:]

If fraction $p$ is parallelizable:

$ upright("Speedup") = frac(1, \( 1 - p \) + p / n) $

where $n$ is number of parallel workers.

#strong[\3. Caching Strategy]

Cache node outputs:

$ upright("cache") : \( v \, s \) arrow.r upright("output") $

#strong[Cache Hit Rate:]

$ upright("Hit Rate") = upright("Cache Hits") / upright("Total Queries") $

#strong[Expected Speedup:]

$ T_(upright("avg")) = h dot.op T_(upright("cache")) + \( 1 - h \) dot.op T_(upright("compute")) $

where $h$ is hit rate, typically
$T_(upright("cache")) lt.double T_(upright("compute"))$.

#strong[Cache Size vs. Hit Rate:]

LRU cache with size $C$:

$ h \( C \) = 1 - e^(- lambda C) $

for Poisson-distributed queries with rate $lambda$.

#strong[\4. State Pruning]

Remove old data:

$ s_(upright("pruned")) = { x in s : upright("age") \( x \) < tau } $

#strong[Information Retention:]

$ I_(upright("retained")) = frac(H \( s_(upright("pruned")) \), H \( s \)) $

where $H$ is information entropy.

#strong[\5. Batch Processing]

Process $b$ requests together:

$ T_(upright("batch")) \( b \) = T_(upright("setup")) + b dot.op T_(upright("per-item")) $

Amortized cost per item:

$ T_(upright("amortized")) = T_(upright("setup")) / b + T_(upright("per-item")) $

decreases with batch size $b$.

=== Reliability and Fault Tolerance
<reliability-and-fault-tolerance>
#strong[Node Failure Probability:]

If node $v$ has failure rate $lambda_v$:

$ P \( upright("fail in time ") t \) = 1 - e^(- lambda_v t) $

#strong[Graph Reliability:]

For path $\( v_1 \, dots.h \, v_n \)$:

$ P \( upright("success") \) = product_(i = 1)^n \( 1 - p_i \) $

where $p_i$ is failure probability of $v_i$.

#strong[Redundancy:]

Execute $k$ parallel nodes, succeed if $gt.eq 1$ succeeds:

$ P \( upright("success") \) = 1 - product_(i = 1)^k p_i $

For identical nodes with $p_i = p$:

$ P \( upright("success") \) = 1 - p^k $

#strong[Mean Time Between Failures (MTBF):]

$ upright("MTBF") = frac(1, sum_(v in V) lambda_v) $

#strong[Recovery Time:]

After failure, restore from checkpoint:

$ T_(upright("recovery")) = T_(upright("detect")) + T_(upright("rollback")) + T_(upright("replay")) $

#strong[Availability:]

$ A = frac(upright("MTBF"), upright("MTBF") + upright("MTTR")) $

where MTTR is mean time to repair.

