=== Advanced Techniques
<advanced-techniques>
#strong[\1. Multi-Task Mixtures:]

Combine instruction data with other training objectives:

$ cal(L)_(upright("total")) = alpha cal(L)_(upright("instruct")) + \( 1 - alpha \) cal(L)_(upright("pretrain")) $

where $alpha in \[ 0.7 \, 0.9 \]$ balances instruction-following with
general knowledge retention.

#strong[\2. Curriculum Learning:]

Train on easy examples first, gradually increasing difficulty:

$ cal(D)^(\( t \)) = { \( I \, x \, y \) : upright("difficulty") \( I \, x \, y \) lt.eq d \( t \) } $

where $d \( t \)$ increases with training step $t$.

#strong[\3. Active Learning for Data Efficiency:]

Select most informative examples for human annotation:

$ upright("score") \( I \, x \) = upright("uncertainty") \( P_theta \( y \| I \, x \) \) + upright("diversity") \( I \, cal(D) \) $

Prioritize high-uncertainty and diverse examples.

