#strong[Embedding Model Selection:]

- #strong[Dimension vs Performance Trade-off:]

  - 384-dim (all-MiniLM-L6-v2): Fast encoding (50ms/text), moderate
    recall\@10 $approx$ 85%

  - 768-dim (SBERT, E5-base): Balanced (100ms/text), recall\@10 $approx$
    91%

  - 1024-dim (BGE-large, E5-large): Best quality (150ms/text),
    recall\@10 $approx$ 95%

  - #emph[Why:] Higher dimensions capture more semantic nuance but
    require more compute and storage

  - #emph[Rule of Thumb:] Use 1024-dim for accuracy-critical
    applications (medical, legal), 384-dim for high-throughput (customer
    support chatbots)

- #strong[Normalization:] ALWAYS L2-normalize before storing in vector
  DB

  - #emph[Why:] Enables cosine similarity via fast dot product:
    $cos \( upright(bold(u)) \, upright(bold(v)) \) = upright(bold(u)) dot.op upright(bold(v))$
    when
    $parallel upright(bold(u)) parallel = parallel upright(bold(v)) parallel = 1$

  - #emph[Performance:] 2-3x speedup over un-normalized cosine
    computation

  - #emph[Implementation:] ‘embeddings / np.linalg.norm(embeddings,
    axis=1, keepdims=True)‘

- #strong[Batch Size for Embedding Generation:]

  - Small texts (\<100 tokens): Batch size = 128-256 (GPU memory
    permitting)

  - Long documents (\>500 tokens): Batch size = 16-32

  - #emph[Compute:] Memory usage $approx$ batch\_size × max\_seq\_len ×
    hidden\_dim × 4 bytes

  - #emph[Example:] Batch=32, seq\_len=512, dim=768 → 32×512×768×4 =
    50MB

- #strong[Similarity Metric Selection:]

  - #strong[Cosine (Default):] Best for semantic search
    (scale-invariant, handles variable document lengths)

  - #strong[Dot Product:] When magnitude matters (e.g., combining
    semantic + relevance score)

  - #strong[Euclidean:] Only for normalized embeddings (equivalent to
    cosine then) or specific domain requirements

  - #emph[Production Standard:] 95% of RAG systems use cosine similarity

#strong[Quick Start Configurations by Use Case:]

- #strong[Medical/Legal Q&A:] BGE-large-1024dim, cosine, top-k=5-10,
  rerank with cross-encoder

- #strong[Customer Support:] all-MiniLM-384dim, cosine, top-k=3, no
  reranking (speed priority)

- #strong[Research Literature:] E5-large-1024dim, cosine, top-k=20,
  aggressive reranking

- #strong[Multi-lingual:] mE5-large, cosine, top-k=10 (handles 100+
  languages)

#strong[Retrieval Quality Benchmarks:]

- #strong[Recall\@5:] Proportion of relevant docs in top-5 results

  - Good: R\@5 $gt.eq$ 0.80 (80% of relevant docs found)

  - Excellent: R\@5 $gt.eq$ 0.90

  - #emph[Impact:] Each 5% drop in recall → 10-15% drop in end-to-end
    answer quality

- #strong[MRR (Mean Reciprocal Rank):] Average 1/rank of first relevant
  document

  - Good: MRR $gt.eq$ 0.60 (relevant doc usually in top-2)

  - Excellent: MRR $gt.eq$ 0.80

  - #emph[Why it matters:] LLMs attend more to earlier context (position
    bias)

