=== Self-RAG (Self-Reflective RAG)
<self-rag-self-reflective-rag>
#strong[Idea:] Model decides when to retrieve and critiques its own
generations.

#strong[Process:]

+ #strong[Retrieval Decision:] Should we retrieve?
  $ P \( upright("retrieve") \| q \) > tau_(upright("retrieve")) $

+ #strong[Generate with Retrieved Context:]
  $ y = upright("LLM") \( q \, upright("context") \) quad upright("if retrieved, else ") y = upright("LLM") \( q \) $

+ #strong[Relevance Check:] Is retrieved content relevant?
  $ P \( upright("relevant") \| q \, upright("context") \) > tau_(upright("rel")) $

+ #strong[Support Check:] Does answer use the context?
  $ P \( upright("supported") \| y \, upright("context") \) > tau_(upright("support")) $

+ #strong[Utility Check:] Is answer useful?
  $ P \( upright("useful") \| q \, y \) > tau_(upright("utility")) $

#strong[Special Tokens:]

- `[Retrieve]`: Trigger retrieval

- `[No Retrieval]`: Generate without retrieval

- `[Relevant]`: Context is relevant

- `[Irrelevant]`: Context not useful

- `[Supported]`: Answer grounded in context

- `[Not Supported]`: Answer not from context

#strong[Training:]

Fine-tune LLM to predict these tokens using critic data:

$ cal(L) = cal(L)_(upright("generation")) + lambda_1 cal(L)_(upright("retrieve")) + lambda_2 cal(L)_(upright("critique")) $

=== RAPTOR (Recursive Abstractive Processing)
<raptor-recursive-abstractive-processing>
#strong[Idea:] Build hierarchical tree of document summaries for
multi-scale retrieval.

#strong[Algorithm:]

#block[
#strong[Input:] Documents ${ d_1 \, dots.h \, d_N }$, LLM $M$
#strong[Output:] Tree structure \/\/ Level 0: Original documents
$upright("nodes")_0 arrow.l { d_1 \, dots.h \, d_N }$ \/\/ Cluster
documents
$upright("clusters") arrow.l upright("GMM-cluster") \( upright("nodes")_(upright("current")) \)$
$upright("nodes")_(upright("next")) arrow.l \[ \]$ \/\/ Summarize
cluster
$s arrow.l M \( upright("“Summarize: ”") + upright("concat") \( C \) \)$
$upright("nodes")_(upright("next")) . upright("append") \( s \)$
$upright("nodes")_(upright("current")) arrow.l upright("nodes")_(upright("next"))$
tree

]
#strong[Retrieval:] Search across all tree levels:

$ upright("retrieve") \( q \) = union.big_(ell = 0)^L upright("top-") k_ell \( upright("sim") \( q \, upright("nodes")_ell \) \) $

#strong[Benefits:]

- High-level summaries for broad questions

- Detailed chunks for specific questions

- Better context coverage

#strong[Implementation:]

```python
