== RAG Best Practices and Optimization
<rag-best-practices-and-optimization>
=== Document Processing
<document-processing>
#strong[Chunking Strategies:]

- #strong[Fixed-size:] Simple, may break semantic units
  $ upright("chunk")_i = upright("doc") \[ i dot.op s : \( i + 1 \) dot.op s + o \] $
  where $s$ is chunk size, $o$ is overlap

- #strong[Semantic:] Split by paragraphs, sections

- #strong[Sentence-aware:] Don't break mid-sentence

- #strong[Context-preserving:] Add parent document context to each chunk

#strong[Optimal Chunk Size:]

Trade-off between granularity and context:

$ upright("Chunk Size") = f \( upright("Query Specificity") \, upright("Context Window") \, upright("Domain") \) $

#strong[Typical ranges:]

- Short queries, specific answers: 256-512 tokens

- Long-form answers: 512-1024 tokens

- Code/structured data: Variable by logical units

=== Query Optimization
<query-optimization>
#strong[Query Expansion:]

$ q' = q + upright("LLM") \( upright("“Rephrase and expand: ”") + q \) $

#strong[Query Decomposition:]

For complex queries, break into sub-questions:

#block[
#strong[Input:] Complex query $q$ #strong[Output:] Final answer
$upright("sub_queries") arrow.l upright("LLM") \( upright("“Break into sub-questions: ”") + q \)$
$a_i arrow.l upright("RAG") \( q_i \)$
$upright("final_answer") arrow.l upright("LLM") \( upright("“Synthesize: ”") + { a_1 \, dots.h \, a_n } \)$
final\_answer

]
=== Context Window Management
<context-window-management>
#strong[Lost-in-the-Middle Problem:]

LLMs attend more to beginning and end of context:

$ upright("Attention") \( i \) prop cases(delim: "{", upright("high") & i in upright("[start, end]"), upright("low") & i in upright("middle")) $

#strong[Solution:] Place most relevant documents at boundaries:

$ upright("Order") = \[ upright("doc")_1 \, upright("doc")_3 \, dots.h \, upright("doc")_(k - 1) \, upright("doc")_2 \] $

where docs are sorted by relevance:
$upright("doc")_1 > upright("doc")_2 > dots.h$

=== Caching and Performance
<caching-and-performance>
#strong[Embedding Cache:]

$ upright("Cache") : upright("hash") \( upright("text") \) arrow.r upright(bold(e m b e d d i n g)) $

Avoid re-computing embeddings for duplicate text.

#strong[Query Cache:]

$ upright("Cache") : upright("hash") \( upright("query") \) arrow.r \( upright("results") \, upright("timestamp") \) $

Cache recent query results with TTL.

