#strong[Key Takeaways - Ray Serve Deployment:]

+ #strong[Replica count from throughput:] Replicas = Target RPS / Single
  Replica RPS. GPT-2 gets 0.5 req/sec per A100, so 4 replicas = 2
  req/sec capacity

+ #strong[Queue size for burst handling:] max\_concurrent\_queries =
  burst\_rate × burst\_duration. Set to 100 for 5 req/sec × 20 sec
  bursts

+ #strong[Async enables batching:] Async handlers allow Ray to batch
  requests on GPU, improving throughput 2-3x vs synchronous

+ #strong[torch.no\_grad() critical:] Saves 70% memory (700MB vs 2GB per
  request), enables 2.8x more concurrent requests on same GPU

+ #strong[Autoscaling saves 60% cost:] Static 20 replicas = \$43K/month,
  autoscaling 2-20 = \$17K/month for same peak capacity

+ #strong[Downscale delay prevents thrashing:] 600-second delay avoids
  constant replica churn, reduces wasted startup costs

