=== Model Access Control
<model-access-control>
#strong[The Problem:]

LLMs are valuable intellectual property. A fine-tuned medical LLM
represents:

- Months of data curation and annotation

- Weeks of expensive GPU training (\$100K+ compute cost)

- Domain expertise embedded in training data

Unauthorized access could lead to:

- Model theft (competitors reverse-engineering)

- Data leakage (extracting training data)

- Misuse (deploying for unintended purposes)

#strong[Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):]

Define access levels:

+ #strong[Data Scientist:] Can view models, run evaluations, cannot
  deploy

+ #strong[ML Engineer:] Can deploy to staging, cannot deploy to
  production

+ #strong[Platform Admin:] Can deploy to production, manage access
  controls

+ #strong[End User (API):] Can query deployed models, rate-limited
  access

