+ #strong[Infrastructure Essentials:]

  - #strong[Training:] Kubernetes for orchestration, fault tolerance
    critical (95% failure probability over 60 days)

  - #strong[Serving:] Ray Serve or Triton for autoscaling, dynamic
    batching

  - #strong[Monitoring:] Prometheus + Grafana for metrics, InfluxDB for
    time-series

+ #strong[Security and Compliance:]

  - Implement RBAC from day 1 (harder to add retroactively)

  - Audit logs cost \$20-50/year but prevent \$100K+ regulatory fines

  - API rate limiting prevents abuse and cost overruns

+ #strong[Latency SLAs by Application:]

  - Interactive chatbot: p95 \< 500ms

  - Code completion: p95 \< 200ms (users expect real-time)

  - Document summarization: p95 \< 5s (batch processing acceptable)

+ #strong[Model Versioning is Non-Negotiable:]
  $ upright("Version") = upright("Model ID") + upright("Training Data Hash") + upright("Hyperparameters") $
  Every production model must be reproducible. Cannot debug issues
  without knowing exact training configuration.

+ #strong[Production Checklist Before Deployment:]

  - Baseline metrics established (accuracy, latency, cost)

  - Drift detection configured (weekly runs)

  - Alerting thresholds tuned (1-2 alerts/month target)

  - Rollback plan tested (\< 5 min revert time)

  - Audit logging enabled (GDPR/HIPAA compliance)

  - Cost monitoring dashboard (track \$/1K requests)

  - Autoscaling configured (2-20 replicas based on load)

  - Model registry entry created (version, lineage, metrics)

  - Security scanning completed (API keys, access control)

  - Load testing passed (1000 concurrent requests)

+ #strong[Human Feedback Integration:]

  Automated metrics capture only 60-70% of model quality. Human feedback
  (thumbs up/down, reports) is essential for:

  - Detecting subtle quality degradation (helpfulness, tone)

  - Identifying edge cases for retraining data

  - Measuring alignment with user expectations

  Collect feedback on 1-5% of responses for continuous improvement.

+ #strong[Cost vs Quality Trade-Off:]

  For a 70B parameter model serving 10M requests/month:

  - FP16 baseline: \$50K/month compute, 92% accuracy

  - INT8 quantized: \$25K/month compute, 90% accuracy

  - INT4 quantized: \$12.5K/month compute, 85% accuracy

  Choose based on application requirements. Medical diagnosis: use FP16.
  Chatbot recommendations: INT8 is fine.

